<v News>新しい組織が集めた情報を、政府がどのように政策に生かしていくのか、これからの働きが注目されています。

00:11:41.447 --> 00:11:45.480
<v Host>Time for a short quiz. Listen and try to answer.

00:11:46.080 --> 00:11:58.703
<v Slow>きのう7月31日に発足した、情報を集めて分析する新しい組織の名前は、何ですか。

00:11:59.504 --> 00:12:05.504
<v Host>The National Intelligence Bureau, created out of the former cabinet intelligence office.

00:12:06.104 --> 00:12:14.000
<v Slow>国家情報局では、およそ何人の職員が働いていますか。

00:12:14.799 --> 00:12:19.504
<v Host>About seven hundred thirty people, working in seven departments.

00:12:20.104 --> 00:12:43.936
<v Host>That's all for today. Japan launched its new National Intelligence Bureau on July thirty-first, bringing together security and diplomatic intelligence that used to be scattered across many agencies. It has about seven hundred thirty staff, and it supports a new council led by the prime minister that met for the first time the same day. Thanks for listening, and see you tomorrow.

00:12:44.535 --> 00:12:46.936
<v News>また明日。
